This project builds on the OpenAI mathematics repository, specifically result
#115 and its sampling and counting manuscripts, pinned at commit
fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb.
Upstream: https://github.com/openai/math
Upstream license: Apache License, Version 2.0.

The 115/ directory preserves the initial GPT-6.1 Sol review and its finite
audit artifacts, provided by Ben Gould on October 8, 2026. It contains
research hypotheses, not a certificate of the complete upstream proof.
Follow-up research and implementation use OpenAI Codex assistance.
Classical dynamic programming, concentration inequalities, and cycle heat-bath
moves are not claimed as newly invented by this project.

The completion-oracle dilation construction uses the classical adjacent-cycle
lattice geometry of Dyer, Kannan, and Mount, Sampling Contingency Tables
(1997), Section 4. The public derivation and verification records distinguish
that geometry from this project's finite-lattice codec and application to
the smaller physical-chain scales.
